From 182cd61fc0dcc75cbb21983e8be983bc39818f36 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Ville=20Kivela=CC=88?= <vkivela@hotmail.com>
Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 23:02:38 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 07/12] extensions: let an extension ask the application to
 open a page

tabs.create and windows.create arrive where a page's own window.open()
arrives, through AddNewContents and adoptNewWindow, so the application
decides what opening a page means with its own surfaces and its own
rules. Declining is an error the extension is told about rather than a
call that never returns.

The page is handed over before it is navigated. Navigating first builds
its render view while the view still has no client, and the adoption then
walks into a view delegate that was never set, which is a crash in
RenderViewHostChanged rather than a warning.

Bitwarden reaches this when its popup asks to open in a window of its
own, which is how its settings are shown: it has no options page, only
routes inside the popup document.

